01:52:49,840 --> 01:52:55,800
 And we forget that most of us haven't been provided that amount of output opportunities

1614
01:52:55,800 --> 01:53:01,400
 to figure out what we think, something that is well-worded that you hear is the product

1615
01:53:01,400 --> 01:53:07,120
 of a lot of thinking and a lot of output, usually a lot more output than you think.

1616
01:53:07,120 --> 01:53:11,960
 One of the things our company did was study the high impact activities that help people

1617
01:53:11,960 --> 01:53:14,480
 achieve clarity in their thinking.

1618
01:53:14,480 --> 01:53:17,440
 And we developed an exercise called essence writing.

1619
01:53:17,440 --> 01:53:18,840
 So here's how it works.

1620
01:53:18,840 --> 01:53:21,160
 Open up a note document or Google Doc.

1621
01:53:21,160 --> 01:53:25,240
 In every night before bed, set a timer for five minutes and you're going to pick a topic

1622
01:53:25,240 --> 01:53:29,960
 you struggle to articulate and just start writing about it in three stages.

1623
01:53:29,960 --> 01:53:36,920
 You're going to do this in 100 words, in 50 words, and then in 25 words.

1624
01:53:36,920 --> 01:53:41,960
 You can use a word counter to track the word count or just use this Google template and

1625
01:53:41,960 --> 01:53:43,920
 it'll be linked below this video.

1626
01:53:43,920 --> 01:53:48,480
 What this does, writing out your thought in three sections, is it trains yourself to

1627
01:53:48,480 --> 01:53:55,200
 develop an internal compass of what a lean, clear answer feels like.

1628
01:53:55,200 --> 01:53:59,240
 So here's an example of something that I was writing last night, never mind the topic.

1629
01:53:59,240 --> 01:54:04,760
 Essence writing is all about taking that archaeological brush and brushing off the layers

1630
01:54:04,760 --> 01:54:08,680
 of dust to reveal the bones of your thought.

1631
01:54:08,680 --> 01:54:14,560
 And when you do this, multiple times, slowly you begin to find a connection between different

1632
01:54:14,560 --> 01:54:19,800
 ideas and this builds a skeleton of the world that makes sense that you can articulate

1633
01:54:19,800 --> 01:54:20,800
 when you speak.

